        <h2 class="heading-lg measure">Compliance basics</h2>
        <p>
          This is the operating rule we build to, not a legal opinion. If your
          counsel wants a different line, we follow that.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>10DLC registration.</strong> Carriers treat business texts from
          a normal 10-digit number as application-to-person traffic. That traffic
          has to be registered, a brand and a campaign, before it is reliable.
          Unregistered texts get filtered. We register before the first customer
          text goes out. You do not buy a number and hope.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Consent.</strong> The person called you. The text is a reply
          about that call. It identifies the business, says you missed them, and
          includes a way to stop. Reply STOP and the thread ends. A missed call
          is not consent to drop that number onto a promotion list, a review
          request blast, or a newsletter. Those need their own opt-in.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not send the text until you have read the wording and signed off,
          the same gate we use before a voice build takes a live customer call.
        </p>

